id: pm-vcs-testenv
title: Isolate test children and provenance from ambient agent sessions
description: "Test environments select explicit operational keys and deliberate fixture overrides. Remove ambient Claude Code, Codex, AI_AGENT and PM_AGENT session state before SDK imports. Retain runner-owned coverage for native production workers and tools; disposable fixtures explicitly disable it. Audit module code and embedded worker programs and compare real provenance in clean and contaminated sessions."
type: Issue
status: in_progress
priority: 2
tags: []
created_at: "2026-10-26T06:40:36.026Z"
updated_at: "2026-10-26T07:44:51.902Z"
author: codex-agent
acceptance_criteria: The three reported annotation/bisect cases produce the same results under clean and contaminated sessions; all child launch sites use explicit environments without host spreads; exact npm/Bun release gates pass.
comments[5]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-10-26T06:40:40.032Z",codex-agent,"Reproduced all three reported failures before changes by injecting synthetic CLAUDECODE, CLAUDE_CODE_*, CODEX_*, AI_AGENT and PM_AGENT_* values: 0/3 pass, actual harness claude-code versus expected codex. Keep exact provenance assertions. Introduce a pure child-environment allowlist plus an entrypoint normalizer before SDK imports; permit deliberate fixture overrides and preserve parent V8 instrumentation separately. Audit direct, aliased and namespaced child-process launches, including previously implicit environments; do not copy host process.env. Run the same three real cases in clean and contaminated children and guard future launches structurally."
  "2026-10-26T07:08:44.975Z",codex-agent,"Round-5 hermeticity: 96 test entrypoints install an operational-key allowlist before SDK imports; 136 child launch sites now carry explicit environments, including 56 previously implicit launches. Fixture identity remains explicit. Parent V8 instrumentation and runner context survive; children disable coverage and omit runner context. Node 22 contaminated-session regression 4/4 and copied-checkout/PM-context cases 2/2 pass. Three actual provenance cases pass 3/3 in clean and contaminated runs. Isolated revert proof: restoring only host-copy behavior in testEnvironment fails 0/3 with claude-code instead of codex; restoring the allowlist passes 3/3. Disabling only isolateTestSession fails its contamination/coverage regression 0/1; restoring passes 1/1. Source/test typecheck, strict lint, 86-source docstrings and zero duplication pass. No dependency changes. Full npm/Bun evidence will come from exact-head CI."
  "2026-10-26T07:33:41.261Z",codex-agent,"Exact-head CI run 40284212531: Node 26 passed all 1990 tests with zero failures/skips, but production coverage failed because the new child builder suppressed runner instrumentation used by direct production-tool and native worker regressions. Correcting the operational allowlist to retain runner-owned NODE_V8_COVERAGE while existing fixture discard overrides remain explicit; no agent-session keys are admitted. Will prove the instrumentation boundary with the real duplication launcher and rerun affected targeted coverage before a new exact-head CI gate."
  "2026-10-26T07:43:06.123Z",codex-agent,"Coverage correction: initial CI passed 1990/1990 on both Node 22 and 26, with zero failed/skipped/cancelled tests, but runner instrumentation was dropped from direct tools and workers. NODE_V8_COVERAGE is now an explicit operational allowlist key; fixture discard overrides remain authoritative. Real duplication launcher targeted coverage passes 100/100/100/100. The audit now includes generated worker source: 96 entrypoints, 150 child launch sites, three embedded programs. New isolated revert proofs: dropping only instrumentation makes the real production-tool collection test fail 0/1 (restored 1/1); removing one embedded consumer environment makes the structural audit fail 0/1 (restored 1/1). Native process-policy and real-tool cases pass 2/2. All helpers were restored before checks."
  "2026-10-26T07:44:50.126Z",codex-agent,"Correction validation complete: environment/provenance/instrumentation suite 5/5 on Node 22 with synthetic session variables and 5/5 through pm test; all 150 audited launches include three embedded worker programs, which must parse before inspection. Native policy plus real tool 2/2, duplication-launcher focused coverage 100/100/100/100, and real built/packed Node/Bun plus project-installed CLI consumers 6/6. Source/test typecheck, strict lint, zero duplication and 86-source/518-declaration docstrings pass at unchanged thresholds. The extra regression preserves instrumentation without admitting session namespaces. Next: archive/commit/accept and new exact-head full CI."
